@startuml sequence-submission
title Sequence Diagram — Workflow A: Submission-to-Decision

actor Citizen
participant "Web Client\n(React)" as UI
participant "Receipt Service" as RS
participant "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB
participant "Ingestion Service" as IS
participant "Linking Service" as LS
participant "Moderator" as MOD
participant "Web Client\n(Public)" as PUB

== Phase 1: Citizen Submits View ==

Citizen -> UI: Select bill, write submission
UI -> RS: POST /receipts
RS -> DB: Lock chain head (SERIALIZABLE)
RS -> RS: Compute SHA-256 hash
RS -> DB: INSERT participation_receipt
RS -> DB: INSERT audit_log
RS --> UI: Receipt ID + timestamp + status
UI --> Citizen: Show receipt confirmation

== Phase 2: Committee Report Tabled ==

note over IS: Triggered by scheduled sync\nor clerk upload
IS -> IS: Fetch/download PDF
IS -> IS: Try native text extraction
alt Text layer insufficient
  IS -> IS: Rasterize pages
  IS -> IS: Run Tesseract OCR
end
IS -> DB: INSERT committee_report
IS -> IS: Parse into entries
IS -> DB: INSERT report_entries (per clause)
IS -> DB: UPDATE extraction_status

== Phase 3: Linking Engine Proposes Matches ==

LS -> DB: Fetch open receipts for bill
LS -> DB: Fetch report entries for bill
LS -> LS: Step 1: Clause-reference match
alt Clause match found
  LS -> LS: confidence = 0.9+
else No clause match
  LS -> LS: Step 2: Text similarity (rapidfuzz)
  LS -> LS: confidence = 0.3-0.89
end
LS -> DB: INSERT submission_match (reviewer_decision = pending)
LS -> LS: Generate explanation

== Phase 4: Moderator Reviews ==

MOD -> UI: View match queue
UI -> LS: GET /matches/pending
LS -> DB: SELECT pending matches
LS --> UI: Match details + explanation
MOD -> UI: Confirm or reject
UI -> LS: POST /matches/{id}/confirm
LS -> DB: UPDATE reviewer_decision = confirmed
LS -> DB: INSERT audit_log

== Phase 5: Public Sees Outcome ==

PUB -> UI: View bill page
UI -> DB: Fetch confirmed matches
DB --> UI: Matches with treatments
UI -> UI: Compute outcome counts
UI --> PUB: Show outcome trail\n(adopted/amended/rejected/not addressed)

@enduml
